# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# This is a security control as much as a speed one: everything listed here would
# otherwise be uploaded to the daemon and could end up in an image layer. A .env
# baked into a layer stays recoverable from the image even if a later layer
# deletes it, and `keys/` holds signing material.

# Secrets and key material — never in an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
keys/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Dependencies are installed inside the build, not copied in. Copying a
# host node_modules would also drag in native modules built for the host's libc,
# which breaks on Alpine's musl.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# Tests and fixtures are not shipped. The fixtures contain generated private keys.
tests/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# The two scripts that read tests/fixtures/, which is excluded just above. In an
# image they could only fail on a file that is not there — and seed-demo.js writes
# fabricated medicine records to a ledger that has no undo, which is not a tool to
# leave lying around inside a deployment. scripts/issue-api-key.js is deliberately
# kept: issuing a real key needs nothing but the database.
scripts/seed-demo.js
scripts/make-dev-keys.js

# Local tooling and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Documentation and scratch space
*.md
!README.md
docs/
scripts/dev/
tmp/
*.log
